msgid "What are the main gaps in publicly financed coverage?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Main gaps in coverage"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A large share of the population (15%) is uninsured and only has access to a "
"few publicly financed health services. This is because access to National "
"Health Insurance Fund benefits is based on the payment of contributions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"National Health Insurance Fund coverage of outpatient medicines, medical "
"products and dental care is limited. Medicine prices are high compared to "
"other countries."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Heavy percentage of co-payments for outpatient prescriptions and inadequate "
"protection from co-payments, especially for poorer households and people "
"with chronic conditions. More than half of all prescriptions financed by "
"the National Health Insurance Fund incur a percentage co-payment of 50% or "
"more of the reference price. There are no exemptions from these "
"co-payments. There is no annual cap on all co-payments."
msgstr ""

msgid "How can Bulgaria strengthen financial protection?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ensure the National Health Insurance Fund covers the whole population"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Government should begin to pay social health insurance contributions "
"for people living below the poverty line who are not entitled to social "
"support. It should also stop penalizing non-payment of contributions by "
"restricting access to health care; addressing non-payment of contributions "
"should be the responsibility of the tax agency rather than the National "
"Health Insurance Fund."
msgstr ""

msgid "Strengthen protection from user charges"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Exempt households with lower incomes and people with chronic conditions "
"from co-payments. Introduce an annual income-based cap on all co-payments. "
"Change percentage co-payments for medicines to low-fixed co-payments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Improve medicines policy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Improve the capacity of the National Health Insurance Fund to purchase "
"outpatient medicines. Continue to reduce medicine prices. Make sure health "
"care providers and pharmacies have incentives to prescribe and dispense the "
"cheapest alternatives."
msgstr ""

msgid "Increase public spending on health"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Support these policy changes by increasing the level of government budget "
"transfers to the National Health Insurance Fund over time. Use additional "
"resources carefully to meet equity and efficiency goals."
msgstr ""

